Experiment 6(b)
Title: Display the lines between start and end line numbers using shell script passed as arguments.  

Steps:
Open terminal.  
Create the script: nano expt6b.sh  
Enter:
#!/bin/bash
start="$1"
end="$2"
file="$3"
sed -n "${start},${end}p" "$file"
```[span_3](start_span)[span_3](end_span)

Save and exit the file: Ctrl + O \rightarrow Enter \rightarrow Ctrl + X  
Execute the script by passing the starting line, ending line and file name:
bash lines.sh 3 7 lines.sh (or bash expt6b.sh 3 7 lines.sh)  
The script displays all the lines from line 3 to line 7 of lines.sh.  




